-- examples/checks/agg-join-delta-first-persp.rofl — A PERSPECTIVE VARIABLE READ UNBOUND STAYS UNBOUND.
--
-- concludes[P](R, Rel) with P unbound does not range over the kernel's books, and in written
-- order nothing has bound P when it is read, so negated_under(concludes, P) (P = $kernel)
-- meets no row and r is empty. A plan from the news of negated_under binds P = $kernel first
-- and then reads the kernel's concludes: 33 rows. A premise with a perspective variable is
-- placed where that variable is bound, or not, as written (agg_breaks `delta_first_persp`).
r(R, Rel, P) :- concludes[P](R, Rel), negated_under(concludes, P).
jdp_kernel(R, Rel) :- r(R, Rel, _).
alarm(jdp_kernel).
